The '''nature impling''' is an [[impling]] that can be caught in the [[Impetuous Impulses]] [[minigame]]. They are located throughout [[Puro-Puro]] and [[Gielinor]]. The player needs at least 58 [[Hunter]] to capture this type of impling with a [[butterfly net]] or [[magic butterfly net]], or 68 Hunter to capture it barehanded. Capturing a nature impling will grant the player either 34 (if caught on Puro-Puro) or 36 (if caught elsewhere in Gielinor) Hunter experience. If there's an empty [[impling jar]] in the player's inventory, this produces a [[nature impling jar]], otherwise the impling is looted immediately.

When the impling is caught, the player can loot the resulting jar to receive an item or trade it with [[Elnock Inquisitor]]. The player can either purchase 3 [[impling jar]]s for one nature impling or, along with 3 [[essence impling]]s and 2 [[eclectic impling]]s, purchase a [[jar generator]] or fully recharge it if they already own it.

==Rarity==
{{Main|Impling#Spawn_mechanics}}
On the Gielinor surface, nature implings have a 20/100 chance to appear out of a mid-tier invisible spawn, as well as a 10/101 chance of appearing out of a high-tier invisible spawn. In Puro-Puro however, nature implings have a 150/301 chance to emerge from one of the high-tier invisible spawns.

For a more detailed breakdown of impling spawn mechanics, see the main article.

